AUD:E_0902{date:"2026-09-24T18:01:21Z", event:"E-0902", task:"T-014", kind:"task_complete", agent:"alfred", result:"Scope 1 (entry_bytes fidelity): _crud.py crud_add now returns entry_text rendered via _format_entry — the exact function write_cortex_from_json uses per entry, byte-identical to disk (quoting normalization, ', ' separators, multi-line cuerpo form); set only on success/dry_run. entry_add_handler reads entry_text with raw-render fallback; bytes_written/entry_bytes/applied now reflect actual serialized bytes (verified live: unquoted input goal:Retro,status:current -> 43B disk, entry_bytes=43). Scope 2 (sibling semantics): chose DOCUMENTATION over re-alignment (repurposing bytes_written would be breaking; mutation size unavailable in _read_and_mutate) — file_bytes added to entry_update/delete/move, cortex.gc, cortex.write + docstring notes + schema descriptions naming the divergence. 10 tests in tests/test_t014_entry_bytes.py asserting byte-exactness against real disk content. Heimdall audit APPROVED (unconditional); Alfred verified pytest 1507 passed 14 skipped 0 failed + ruff clean. Non-blocking audit notes: entry_text parasitic fidelity (reconstructed dict vs appended doc entry), crud_add docstring doesn't document new key, cortex.write schema doesn't name divergence, cortex.file.validate has same ambiguity class.", evidence:"Scope 1 (entry_bytes fidelity): _crud.py crud_add now returns entry_text rendered via _format_entry — the exact function write_cortex_from_json uses per entry, byte-identical to disk (quoting normalization, ', ' separators, multi-line cuerpo form); set only on success/dry_run. entry_add_handler reads entry_text with raw-render fallback; bytes_written/entry_bytes/applied now reflect actual serialized bytes (verified live: unquoted input goal:Retro,status:current -> 43B disk, entry_bytes=43). Scope 2 (sibling semantics): chose DOCUMENTATION over re-alignment (repurposing bytes_written would be breaking; mutation size unavailable in _read_and_mutate) — file_bytes added to entry_update/delete/move, cortex.gc, cortex.write + docstring notes + schema descriptions naming the divergence. 10 tests in tests/test_t014_entry_bytes.py asserting byte-exactness against real disk content. Heimdall audit APPROVED (unconditional); Alfred verified pytest 1507 passed 14 skipped 0 failed + ruff clean. Non-blocking audit notes: entry_text parasitic fidelity (reconstructed dict vs appended doc entry), crud_add docstring doesn't document new key, cortex.write schema doesn't name divergence, cortex.file.validate has same ambiguity class.", cycle:"CYCLE-12"}

